Write the Danaco Nurt program that does the same as this PowerShell command:

$py = if ($IsWindows) { 'python' } else { 'python3' }
while (-not (Test-Path data/export.csv)) { Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force backup | Out-Null
Copy-Item data/export.csv backup/export-5.csv

In inventory/store.py, replace this block:
def find_item(items, sku):
    for item in items:
        if item.sku == sku:
            return item
    return None

with this block:
def find_item(items, sku):
    return next((item for item in items if item.sku == sku), None)

Write the Danaco Nurt program that does the same as this PowerShell command:

$p = Join-Path $PWD 'src/format.ts'
$t = [IO.File]::ReadAllText($p)
$old = 'export function formatDate(value: Date): string {
  console.log("formatting", value);
  return value.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
}
'.Replace("`n", "`r`n")
$new = 'export function formatDate(value: Date): string {
  return value.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
}
'.Replace("`n", "`r`n")
if (([regex]::Matches($t, [regex]::Escape($old))).Count -ne 1) { throw 'expected one match' }
[IO.File]::WriteAllText($p, $t.Replace($old, $new))
